  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Added support for integration with .NET applications (e.g., ASP.NET, WinUI3, MAUI, etc.) via new fluent interfaces and methods, such as:\n\t\t\t- IoC.Configuration.DiContainerBuilder.FileBased.IIntegratesWithHostBuilder\n\t\t\t- IoC.Configuration.DiContainerBuilder.FileBased.IRegisterModulesWithHostBuilder\n\t\t\t- IoC.Configuration.DiContainerBuilder.IApplicationHostBuilder\n\n\t\t\tThese changes allow for easy configuration of applications to use IoC.Configuration containers when resolving classes via application containers.\n\n\t\t\tSee example projects in the solution for implementation details:\n\t\t\t- ApplicationIntegrationDemos.ASP.NET.WebApi/WebApiDemo/WebApiDemo.csproj\n\t\t\t- ApplicationIntegrationDemos/Maui/MauiDemo/MauiDemo.csproj\n\t\t\t- ApplicationIntegrationDemos/WinUI3/WinUI3Demo/WinUI3Demo.csproj\n\n\t\t\tNuGet packages \"IoC.Configuration.AspNet\" and \"IoC.Configuration.Maui\" provide extensions for specific application types.\n\n\t\t\tNOTE: Currently, application extension is supported for file-based configuration only. Code-based configuration support may be added in the future based on demand.\n\n\t\t\tFramework Support (new versions of IoC.Configuration.Autofac and IoC.Configuration.Ninject will be published soon):\n\t\t\t- IoC.Configuration.Autofac v2.2.0: Full implementation for application support.\n\t\t\t- IoC.Configuration.Ninject v2.2.1: Provides interface stubs that throw NotImplementedException. Support will be completed once the Ninject library implements Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.IServiceProviderFactory<TContainerBuilder>",
